  "result": "Perfect! All 134 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the date handling module:\n\n**Created `src/dates.js`** with three UTC-based date functions:\n- `isValidDate(text)` \u2014 validates that text is a real date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n  - Uses `T00:00:00Z` for UTC timezone\n  - Rejects invalid dates like 2025-02-30\n  - Accepts leap year dates correctly\n\n- `addDays(date, n)` \u2014 adds n days to a date (can be negative)\n  - Uses UTC date arithmetic with `setUTCDate()`\n  - Handles year/month boundaries correctly\n  - Works with both positive and negative values\n\n- `daysBetween(a, b)` \u2014 calculates the difference in whole days (b - a)\n  - Uses UTC timestamps\n  - Returns negative value if b < a\n  - Correctly handles leap years and year boundaries\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Removed local `isValidDate` function\n- Imported and uses `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Maintains UTC date handling consistently\n\n**Created `test/dates.test.js`** with 16 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Valid and invalid date formats\n- Invalid date values (Feb 30, month 13, etc.)\n- Leap year handling (2024 is leap, 2025 is not)\n- Adding positive, negative, and large day values\n- Year and month boundary crossings\n- daysBetween calculations across years and with leap years\n- Consistency checks between addDays and daysBetween\n- Integration with createInvoice\n\nAll 134 tests pass (118 previous + 16 new). The dates module ensures all date arithmetic is done in UTC, never in local time zones.",
